    "_readme":  "EXAMPLE manifest (a cute-animal demo set). To use your own pack: copy this file to pack.json in this folder, replace the cards with your own names/stats/skills, and drop your images next to it. Cards are full-art by default: the image IS the card and the game only overlays cost/attack/health badges. Skills and effects are matched by name against the registries in @tcg/shared. rarity (LEGENDARY/EPIC/RARE/COMMON) sets each card's pull-weight tier when you mint the pack on TigerMint — run `npm run mint-pack` to launch this exact file as a real drop. Two optional per-card fields: description (flavor text, max 500 chars, minted as the item description and shown as card text locally) and editions (that card's print run — how many copies exist in the drop; rarity-tier defaults apply when absent). Deck access follows rarity: COMMON (or unset) cards form the basic deck everyone plays free; RARE/EPIC/LEGENDARY cards are mint-only — players must pull the NFT to play them (they show locked in the deck builder until owned). A per-card boolean `basic` overrides that rule either way (see Snowshoe Archer: a rare kept free). pack.json and your images are gitignored, so your pack stays local unless you choose to commit it.",
